{"crc":"b5ecbbb3","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at this bug, the issue is in the `FigureCanvasMac.resize` method in `backend_macosx.py`. When a figure is unpickled, the `resize` method is called, and it's dividing by `self.device_pixel_ratio` which causes the DPI to double on M1 Macs.\n\nThe problem is that `device_pixel_ratio` is not properly initialized when the canvas is created during unpickling. The fix should ensure that `device_pixel_ratio` is properly set to 1.0 when the canvas is initialized.\n\nHere's the fix:\n\n# path: lib/matplotlib/backends/backend_macosx.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    def __init__(self, figure):\n        super().__init__(figure=figure)\n        self._draw_pending = False\n        self._is_drawing = False\n=======\n    def __init__(self, figure):\n        super().__init__(figure=figure)\n        self._draw_pending = False\n        self._is_drawing = False\n        self.device_pixel_ratio = 1.0\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":2},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQBTW9XW36JX7N92Q20GYVJ","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQBTW9SJRSGAFYG27ZK7XF5"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":20,"t":1786416822.695979}
